  "id": "selective-potentiation",
  "term": "selective potentiation",
  "definition": "Selective potentiation is the strengthening of some neural connections rather than others according to patterns of firing activity. In the source, it refers to spike-timing-dependent plasticity preferentially increasing connections with particular transmission delays, especially during oscillatory input.",
